---
import Base from "../../layouts/Base.astro";
---

<Base
  title="Blabb Terms of Use — Biotite Solutions"
  description="Terms governing use of the Blabb Android application."
>
  <section class="section wrap">
    <div class="split">
      <div>
        <p class="eyebrow">Blabb</p>
        <h1 class="t-display t-2xl">Terms of use</h1>
        <p>Effective August 15, 2026</p>
      </div>
      <div class="prose">
        <p>
          These Terms govern use of the Blabb Android application, developed
          and published by Joseph Samara. By using Blabb, you agree to these
          Terms. If you do not agree, do not use the application.
        </p>

        <h2 class="t-lg">The service</h2>
        <p>
          Blabb is a local speech-to-text utility that records audio when the
          user starts dictation, transcribes it on the device, and attempts to
          insert the resulting text into a text field selected by the user.
          Blabb has no account service and does not provide cloud storage.
        </p>

        <h2 class="t-lg">Your responsibilities</h2>
        <p>
          Use Blabb only for lawful purposes and only on devices and content you
          are authorized to use. You are responsible for obtaining any consent
          required before recording another person's speech. Do not use Blabb
          to violate privacy, intellectual-property, communications, or other
          applicable laws, or to interfere with another app or device.
        </p>

        <h2 class="t-lg">Review before sending</h2>
        <p>
          Speech recognition and punctuation are probabilistic and can be
          inaccurate, incomplete, or inappropriate for the context. Always
          review dictated text before sending, publishing, signing, or relying
          on it. Blabb is not intended for emergency communications or for
          creating unreviewed medical, legal, financial, safety-critical, or
          similarly consequential content.
        </p>

        <h2 class="t-lg">Android permissions and other apps</h2>
        <p>
          Blabb's bubble and insertion features depend on Android permissions
          and interfaces, including microphone, AccessibilityService,
          notifications, and display-over-other-apps access. Users can pause or
          stop Blabb and can revoke these permissions in Android Settings.
          Android, device manufacturers, keyboards, and destination apps
          control their own text fields and background behavior. Blabb does not
          guarantee compatibility with every field or uninterrupted operation
          after another app or Android changes.
        </p>

        <h2 class="t-lg">Local data and privacy</h2>
        <p>
          Blabb's handling of audio, text-field data, transcripts, diagnostics,
          model downloads, retention, and deletion is described in the
          <a class="link-inline" href="/blabb/privacy/"
            >Blabb Privacy Policy</a
          >.
        </p>

        <h2 class="t-lg">Third-party components</h2>
        <p>
          Blabb includes open-source software, fonts, and speech models governed
          by their respective licenses. Required attributions and license
          information are available under <strong>Open-source licenses</strong>
          in the app. Those components are provided under their own license
          terms.
        </p>

        <h2 class="t-lg">Updates and availability</h2>
        <p>
          Blabb may be updated to improve compatibility, security, performance,
          models, or features. An update may change device requirements or
          require renewed permission or disclosure review. The service or a
          particular compatibility route can be changed or discontinued when
          necessary for security, law, platform requirements, or
          maintainability.
        </p>

        <h2 class="t-lg">Disclaimer</h2>
        <p>
          To the maximum extent permitted by applicable law, Blabb is provided
          "as is" and "as available," without warranties of uninterrupted
          operation, universal compatibility, transcription accuracy, fitness
          for a particular purpose, or non-infringement. Rights that cannot
          lawfully be excluded remain unaffected.
        </p>

        <h2 class="t-lg">Limitation of liability</h2>
        <p>
          To the maximum extent permitted by applicable law, the developer is
          not liable for indirect, incidental, special, consequential, or
          punitive damages, or for loss caused by unreviewed transcription,
          permission changes, destination-app behavior, device failure, or loss
          of local data. This limitation does not exclude liability that
          applicable law does not allow to be excluded.
        </p>

        <h2 class="t-lg">Changes to these Terms</h2>
        <p>
          The effective date will be updated when these Terms change materially.
          Continued use after an updated version becomes available constitutes
          acceptance to the extent permitted by law.
        </p>

        <h2 class="t-lg">Contact</h2>
        <p>
          Questions about these Terms:
          <a class="link-inline" href="mailto:josephsamara00@gmail.com"
            >josephsamara00@gmail.com</a
          >
        </p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>
</Base>
